 "start": {
  "heading": "How to use this guide",
  "paragraphs": [
   "GTA VI came out on 19 November 2026. Rockstar has not published a cheat list, so every input here comes from outlets that tested the game in its first days. We show only what they report, and we say plainly what is not confirmed.",
   "Reported by those outlets: cheats unlock only after you finish the story, and each one also has its own task. To enter one, press Up on the D-pad to open the phone, hold L1 (PS5) or LB (Xbox), press R1 or RB, then press the D-pad sequence. All inputs are D-pad only, so PS5 and Xbox differ just in the shoulder buttons."
  ],
  "cards": [
   {
    "title": "Trophies and saving",
    "text": "Outlets report that using a cheat turns off trophies and achievements and stops saving for that play session. Save first."
   },
   {
    "title": "One wrong press",
    "text": "Several codes differ by one or two presses. A slip can start a different cheat, so enter each one slowly."
   }
  ],
  "checked": "Checked on 20 November 2026 against PowerPyx, GamesRadar+, VICE, Red Bull, Insider Gaming and Dexerto. Most of these lists trace back to the same first source, and none showed independent proof, so no code is marked verified."
 },
 "table": {
  "heading": "Cheat codes for PS5 and Xbox",
  "note": "Enter after the phone: hold L1 or LB, press R1 or RB, then the arrows. Cheats with no input yet are named in the game but have no reliable code."
 },
 "closing": {
  "heading": "Staying safe",
  "cards": [
   {
    "title": "No downloads",
    "text": "A real GTA VI cheat is typed on the controller. Any cheat download, trainer or generator is a scam."
   },
   {
    "title": "Lists change",
    "text": "Inputs are still being checked. Look at the guide page on mayobebros.com for updates."
   }
  ]
 },
